[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   Step 081 -- geocentric observation-direction null.
[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   Any astrometric or observational systematic localized on the sky
[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   (zonal catalogue errors, galactic-plane crowding, twilight geometry)
[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   must act on the direction from which the comet is actually seen --
[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   its geocentric direction near perihelion.  For Oort-spike comets that
[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   direction is dominated by Earth's position at the perihelion epoch,
[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   not by the comet's aphelion: in-cap membership and observed-sky
[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   position are geometrically decoupled.  This step computes each
[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   class-1 CODE comet's geocentric direction at perihelion epoch from
[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   DE440s and tests whether the in-cap cohort's observed directions
[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   cluster -- the necessary condition for a sky-position systematic to
[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   manufacture the cap-correlated anomaly.
[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   Inputs : data/raw/code/code_*.html, data/raw/warsaw/warsaw_tablec.dat,
[2026-09-20 11:46:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 081]   data/raw/spice/de440s.bsp
